# CrystOD: the example files that ship in the wheel (crystod/examples/).
# Read by script/sync_packaged_examples.py, which copies the selected files
# (byte for byte, git-tracked files only) into crystod/examples/ and writes
# crystod/examples/index.json and README. This file itself is not shipped.
#
# One path or glob per line, relative to example/ ('*' does not cross '/',
# '**' matches any number of directories). 'requires A: B C' means that the
# README of A uses files of B and C, so crystod-example copies them along.
# 'budget N' is the maximum total size (bytes) of the packaged files.
#
# Left out on purpose (not in the pip package): large data (the full 41.7 MB
# XDATCAR, every FORCE_CONSTANTS), third-party and debug material (23 debug*,
# AMPLIMODES/ISODISTORT outputs), test_pyscf (POTCAR), generated outputs;
# and the data of unpublished work, which is not distributed at all
# (03 vasp_overlap, vasp_SrTiO3_LAK, 06 CdF2).

budget 8_000_000

requires 29_phonon_activity: 28_phonon_irrep 30_phonon_fatband
requires 40_md_projection: 33_modulation 39_xdatcar2adp
requires 45_python_api: 28_phonon_irrep
